{"name":"Trefoil","hex":"#47562f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"trefoil","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants of the pea family, having compound, trifoliate leaves; especially one of the genus Trifolium.","A symbol having the shape of such leaves, especially when used as an architectural ornament."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trefoil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trefoil","blocks":[{"text":"A trefoil is a graphic form composed of the outline of three overlapping rings, used in architecture, Pagan and Christian symbolism, among other areas. The term is also applied to other symbols with a threefold shape. A similar shape with four rings is called a quatrefoil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Trefoil-Architectural.svg/330px-Trefoil-Architectural.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trefoil"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Evolution_du_plan_des_temples_copie.jpg/120px-Evolution_du_plan_des_temples_copie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Evolution_du_plan_des_temples_copie.jpg/250px-Evolution_du_plan_des_temples_copie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Evolution_du_plan_des_temples_copie.jpg/120px-Evolution_du_plan_des_temples_copie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEvolution_du_plan_des_temples_copie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Trikonchos.gif/120px-Trikonchos.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d7/Trikoncho